# 🚩 Challenge: [Bit-O-Asm-3]
![alt text](bit-o-asm-4.png)
## 📝 Challenge Description
Can you figure out what is in the eax register? Put your answer in the academy flag format: academy{n} where n is the contents of the eax register in the decimal number base. If the answer was 0x11 your flag would be academy{17}. Download the assembly dump here.

Hints:
1. Don't tell anyone I told you this, but you can solve this problem without understanding the compare/jump relationship.

2. Of course, if you're really good, you'll only need one attempt to solve this problem.
---

### Code / Terminal Snippets
```bash
1. wget https://challenge-files.cylabacademy.net/library/b14a53c80d0f28fa842055ab567694917ef71b9f466545c3597aa8940284e212/disassembler-dump0_d.txt
2. cat disassembler-dump0_d.txt
3. echo "ibase=16; 9FE1A - 65" | bc

or 

4. printf "0x%x\n" $((0x9fe1a - 0x65))

```

---

## 🚀 Exploitation / Solution Path
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. Download the `disassembler-dump0_d.txt` file using `wget`.
2. See the content using `cat` command.
3. Convert the register using `echo`  with ibase=16.
4. The flag will be displayed.

